A note specific to this repo, because it matters more here than in most of
this ecosystem's other repos: this license covers OpenEvo's own authored and
compiled content only -- our institutional-actor descriptions, our own
policy-principle statements, our schemas, our documentation. It says nothing
about, and grants no rights to, the underlying Indian government
curriculum/policy documents this repo describes or occasionally quotes from
(NCERT/CBSE textbooks and syllabi, NCF text, state curriculum frameworks,
etc.). Those documents remain under whatever copyright status their own
publishers hold, which this repo's own founding research found to be a
genuinely unresolved legal question for NCERT/CBSE specifically (see
docs/source-notes/2026-09-30-india-curriculum-licensing-landscape-research.md)
-- see each record's own accessTier/licenseOrRightsNote fields, not this
file, for what's actually known or assumed about a specific quoted source.
